; examples-daw harness, the BUILD half. `doc.sjon` is a SYMLINK to
; `examples/daw/piece.sjon` — the native document the shipped `.mid` is
; built from, so the gate compiles the shipped example itself (plan 09:
; "`examples-*` (every shipped example is a symlinked corpus case)";
; pacer 12 D1).
;
; `(export-score)` pins that the document is compose-clean: one
; `(target …)` per target it drives, every lane kind in pacer's
; vocabulary.
;
; `(build :kind mid :cc 1)` is the example's whole claim in one line. The
; `:cc 1` is the `--cc 1` the README's command passes — a native curve
; lane has no controller of its own, so without it `haze` would be
; `render_cc_missing` and ride in the residue alone. The golden carries:
;
;   * the built bytes' length and sha256 — the SAME sha256 the
;     `examples-daw-mid` case's `(fixture …)` line pins over the
;     COMMITTED `examples/daw/piece.mid`, which is how a stale committed
;     artifact shows up as a two-line diff;
;   * `(rung1 :ok true)` — the bytes re-read and re-write identically;
;   * `(rung3 :ok true)` — `dump(build(doc))` is this document again,
;     form for form at the timeline tier. That flag IS the round trip the
;     README claims, asserted rather than described;
;   * one `residue_only` warning, for the query lane a `.mid` cannot
;     hold.
(export-score)
(build :kind mid :cc 1)
